        "\n",
        "## Documentation\n",
        "\n",
        "- Good code tends to come with good *documentation* - written descriptions of what the code does.\n",
        "- In Python, we can include \"comments\" - text that is not evaluated as code - by starting lines with `#`"
      ],
      "id": "4798a4c3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# This is a comment.\n",
        "print(\"This is code.\")\n",
        "# This is another comment."
      ],
      "id": "1c4618ea",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Update `pw.py`\n",
        "\n",
        "- Here is how I documented `pw.py`:"
      ],
      "id": "eb19aaae"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Example of a piecewise function, from a student.\n",
        "# f(x) = 9x^2 + 5 | x < 4\n",
        "#        9        | 4 <= x <= 8\n",
        "#        2 - x    | x > 8\n",
        "def piecewise(x):\n",
        "    if (x < 4):\n",
        "        return 9 * x ** 2 + 5\n",
        "    elif (4 <= x <= 8):\n",
        "        return 9\n",
        "    elif (x > 8):\n",
        "        return 2 - x"
      ],
      "id": "e3e94e0e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- This is functionally indentical, but easier on me!\n",
        "\n",
        "## Updating `tax.py`\n",
        "\n",
